course: dictionary
lesson: 4825
title: Hurricane: a very strong storm
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A hurricane is a very strong storm with violent winds and heavy rain. It forms over warm seas. You can tell how strong it is from its winds: hurricane-force winds blow faster than about 120 kilometres an hour.
explain: Read the clues in «In the middle of a hurricane is the eye, a calm area with light winds and often a clear sky, ringed by the strongest winds of all.» The middle is calm, and the strongest winds are all around it, not in the middle.
explain: The same kind of storm has different names in different places. A storm is a hurricane in the Atlantic, a typhoon near the Philippines and Japan, and a cyclone in the Indian Ocean. If you know one name, you can work out the others.
fact: A hurricane is a very strong storm with violent winds and heavy rain that forms over warm seas.
fact: Hurricane-force winds are winds of more than about 120 kilometres an hour.
fact: The eye is the calm centre of a hurricane, with light winds and often a clear sky.
fact: When a hurricane comes ashore, its winds push the sea up into a wall of water called a storm surge, and this flooding can be more dangerous than the wind itself.
fact: «Hurricane season» is the time of year when hurricanes are most likely to form, and families follow warnings and prepare.
exercise: Where does a hurricane form? | *Over warm seas | On high mountains | Over cold seas | In deserts
exercise: «In the middle of a hurricane is the eye.» What is the eye? | The fiercest winds of all | A wall of sea water | A thunderstorm cloud | *A calm area with light winds and often a clear sky
exercise: Hurricane-force winds blow faster than about how many kilometres an hour? | 50 | 80 | 200 | *120
test: «The same kind of storm is called a typhoon near the Philippines and Japan.» What is that storm called in the Atlantic? | *Hurricane | Cyclone | Typhoon | Blizzard
test: When a hurricane comes ashore, which is often more dangerous? | The wind alone | *The storm surge, a wall of water pushed up by the winds | The sunshine after it | The thunder
exam: Leo reads «the fiercest wind just around the eye». What does fiercest mean? | Warmest | Gentlest | Calmest | *Strongest and most violent
